Summary: The future's so bright, I gotta wear shades...
Keywords: Ascension, Chainsaw Yo-Yo of Yendor, sunglasses

Well, yeah, I ascended, with a Valkyrie, I can tell you're impressed.  I was
happy, though--I beat the high score on the local machine, and the old one 
was established by the guy who *installed* Nethack here.
Sumeria the Lady ascended with 15,461,345 points--yes, I polypiled for gems,
and only for those worth more than 1,000 zorkmids each, no less (I had to
beat the old high score of 13,500,000).  Had 556/556 hp's--the old cursed
Bell of Opening trick has been toned down by the Dev Team, those darn wraiths
show up less often and leave fewer corpses.  *sigh*  Had the old Chainsaw
Yo-Yo of Yendor, of course, which I seldom threw anyway (personal style
combined with a fear of losing the dern thing);  received Vorpy when I became
the Envoy of Balance, and then evaporated it trying to enchant it to +7. =)
It took over a week of late-night delving and lots of polypiling, but I
finally did it.
As to a new item idea--"dark spectacles" which are really "sunglasses."  A
new armor location, over the eyes.  Shades don't give any -ac, but can be
enchanted, like Hawaiian shirts.  Standard pair makes any room, lit or not,
look dark (just the 8 squares around the character visible).  Cursed pair
won't come off (of course) and makes the wearer blind.  Blessed pair--I dunno,
doesn't make the room dark???  Either a blessed or uncursed pair makes the
wearer immune to being blinded (by Archon radiance, magic traps, lightning
blasts, yellow lights, cobra venom, *thrown* potions of blindness--but not
those which are quaffed, etc.).  Thought this up because I got tired of
being blinded by all those lightning blasts which couldn't hit my -71ac.  =)
One could even make a pair of X-ray specs, rarer, of course, that give the
wearer clairvoyance when worn (see right through walls, amaze your friends!).
Whaddaya think, too loopy?  Any idea if the mythical Dev Team reads any of 
these posts?
Happy Hacking....

